%[text] %[text:anchor:T_DEF03274] # DC Circuit Analysis
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_577C7603] ## Scripts
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_BC8955C0] ### [**MeshAnalysis.m**](file:./Scripts/MeshAnalysis.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,430,218]}
%[text] |  | **In this script, students will...** | **Academic disciplines** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Cover image for MeshAnalysis](text:image:8a68) | <p>• Use mesh analysis to compute currents through a linear circuit.</p><p>• Solve the matrix form of circuit equations in MATLAB.</p><p>• Model and analyze linear circuits in Simscape.</p> | • Electrical Engineering |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_17056DF7] ### [**NodalAnalysis.m**](file:./Scripts/NodalAnalysis.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,430,218]}
%[text] |  | **In this script, students will...** | **Academic disciplines** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Cover image for NodalAnalysis](text:image:1390) | <p>• Use nodal analysis to compute voltages.</p><p>• Solve the matrix form of circuit equations in MATLAB.</p><p>• Model and analyze linear circuits in Simscape.</p> | • Electrical Engineering |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_93FB3755] ### [**TheveninNorton.m**](file:./Scripts/TheveninNorton.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,430,218]}
%[text] |  | **In this script, students will...** | **Academic disciplines** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Cover image forTheveninNorton](text:image:07be) | <p>• Explain Thevenin and Norton equivalent circuits.</p><p>• Solve for Thevenin and Norton equivalents.</p><p>• Compare circuits to their Thevenin and Norton equivalents.</p> | • Electrical Engineering |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_D4F9A4D1] ### [**RCCircuits.m**](file:./Scripts/RCCircuits.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,430,218]}
%[text] |  | **In this script, students will...** | **Academic disciplines** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Cover image for RCCircuits](text:image:2037) | <p>• Simulate charging and discharging RC circuits.</p><p>• Plot solutions of RC circuit differential equations.</p><p>• Measure the time constant of an RC circuit.</p> | • Electrical Engineering |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_1E0A6441] ### [**RLCCircuits.m**](file:./Scripts/RLCCircuits.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,448,201]}
%[text] |  | **In this script, students will...** | **Academic disciplines** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Cover image for RLCCircuits](text:image:4b78) | <p>• Compare the response of first and second order circuits.</p><p>• Analyze a second order RLC circuit differential equation.</p><p>• Solve for the natural frequency and damping in an RLC circuit.</p><p>• Compare underdamped, overdamped, and critically damped circuits.</p> | • Electrical Engineering |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E550DF08] ### [**OpAmps.m**](file:./Scripts/OpAmps.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,430,220]}
%[text] |  | **In this script, students will...** | **Academic disciplines** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Cover image for OpAmps](text:image:7c7b) | <p>• Describe the open-loop behavior of an op amp.</p><p>• Compare ideal and non-ideal op amp behavior.</p><p>• Analyze negative feedback op amp circuits.</p><p>• Design circuits using combinations of basic op amp circuits.</p> | • Electrical Engineering |
%[text:table]
